/* Logic

1. Use a **max heap** to store the `k` smallest elements.
2. Traverse every element of the array.
3. Insert the current element into the max heap.
4. If the heap size becomes greater than `k`, remove the **largest element** using `pop()`.
5. After processing all elements, the heap contains exactly the `k` smallest elements.
6. The largest element among these `k` elements (`pq.top()`) is the **kth smallest element**.

**Example:**
`arr = {7, 10, 4, 3, 20, 15}, k = 3`

The heap finally contains `{7, 3, 4}`.

So, `pq.top() = 7` → **3rd smallest element = 7**.

**Time Complexity:** `O(n log k)`
**Space Complexity:** `O(k)`
*/

class Solution {
	public:
	int kthSmallest(vector<int> &arr, int k) {
		// Max heap: largest element stays at the top
		priority_queue<int> pq;
		
		// Traverse through all elements of the array
		for (int i : arr) {
			
			// Add current element to the heap
			pq.push(i);
			
			// Keep only the k smallest elements in the heap
			// If size becomes greater than k, remove the largest element
			if (pq.size() > k)
				pq.pop();
		}
		
		// The largest among the k smallest elements
		// is the kth smallest element
		return pq.top();
	}
};
